## Goal

Use principal component analysis (PCA) to summarize variation among the six bulk RNA-seq samples from the gene count matrix, and plot the samples with points coloured by their condition (untreated or treated). The analysis will provide the first two principal components and the fraction of variance each explains; it will not test differential expression or make claims about statistical significance.

